<drac2>
# ============================================================
# BattleScry alias v0.2.48
# v0.2.48: (1) initiative groups now come back in the link. hasattr does not exist in Draconic, so the
#          group lookup failed silently and BattleScry never saw existing groups. (2) the link from a
#          bootstrap also carries hidden-stat and group info, so monsters open red and grouped.
# v0.2.47: combatants whose names contain ; or | are left out of the link (they would corrupt it)
#          and named in the embed so the DM can rename them.
# v0.2.46: no more false position conflicts when tokens are on the map but no map effect is
#          attached yet. With no baseline at all, the BattleScry edit wins as documented.
# v0.2.45: link embed wording matches the site (Copy for Discord, phones supported) and the
#          Data String - Local Testing field is gone from the public embed.
# v0.2.44: the link from a bootstrap (combat running, no map host yet) now lists the combatants
#          already in initiative, so BattleScry opens with them in the unplaced list.
# v0.2.43: (1) `!bscry help`, or any unknown subcommand, shows usage instead of falling through to
#          the export path and bootstrapping a combat. (2) The map host is remembered by combatant
#          id in combat metadata (bscry_host), so a host renamed BEFORE the first map is attached
#          is still found and no second DM is added. (3) The export skips the real host, whatever
#          it is named, not only a combatant literally called DM; overlay notes addressed to DM
#          land on the host. (4) The three-way-merge BASE is stored per combat and per user in
#          combat metadata (bscry_load_<user id>) instead of one uvar shared by every channel, so
#          running !bscry in a second game no longer invalidates an open session in the first.
#          The old uvar is still written and is the fallback. (5) Links carry ch=<channel id> so
#          BattleScry can tell two games open in one browser apart.
# v0.2.42: the apply embed's map preview is fixed. Avrae memoises SimpleCombatant.attacks on
#          FIRST access per wrapper (AliasStatBlock._attacks) and add_effect() only refreshes
#          .effects, never .attacks. find_map_host() scanned .attacks on every combatant in
#          c.combatants BEFORE the map effect was written, freezing a pre-write snapshot on the
#          exact wrapper objects Croebh's maplib later reads (its load_data() scans
#          combat().combatants[].attacks). Result: get_link() returned None and the embed had no
#          -image on a fresh combat, and would have shown the PRE-apply map on an existing one.
#          Host lookup now uses get_effect("map", True), which reads through to the combatant
#          and memoises nothing, and every read of the map text goes through map_text_of(), which
#          uses a throwaway wrapper. No wrapper in c.combatants has .attacks touched before the
#          write, so maplib memoises post-write state and renders the current map.
# v0.2.41: apply now honours a standalone flag from BattleScry (section 9, `sa`). A BS session
#          opened directly at battlescry.com never sees Avrae's map, so it has no meaningful
#          BASE and its map fields are a DECLARATION, not a diff. Previously those were
#          three-way merged against the `bscry_load` uvar left over from an earlier session,
#          which conflicted on all four map scalars and silently discarded the map the user
#          had just picked. With the flag set, BASE is cleared and Size/Background/Options/View
#          are taken as given. Flag absent (older BS) -> unchanged three-way merge.
# v0.2.40: the host combatant that holds the map effect is now found by looking for the
#          combatant carrying a `map` attack, falling back to the DM/Map/Lair name match.
#          Renaming the host in Avrae after attach no longer orphans the map state (the
#          old name-only lookup would miss it and bootstrap a fresh DM). One shared
#          find_map_host() helper replaces the three identical name loops.
# v0.2.39: the `cs` export param gains a 4th field, the hidden flag (cs=name:cur:max:ac:h), set from
#          cmb.is_hidden, so BattleScry preserves a combatant's hidden-stats state on import.
# v0.2.38: export now includes each combatant's current HP, max HP, and AC in a new `cs` link
#          param (cs=name:cur:max:ac;...), so BattleScry imports those stats instead of blanks.
#          Read from cmb.hp / cmb.max_hp / cmb.ac; any that are None are emitted empty.
# v0.2.37: edits to existing combatants now round-trip. New apply section 8 (ed): each entry
#          name|ac|hpCur|hpMax|init|group carries only the fields BS saw change, replayed as one
#          `!i opt "name" -ac N -hp cur -max maxhp -p init -group G` (changed flags only). Counted
#          in the applied-summary as "N updated combatant(s)". Section absent (older BS) -> skipped.
# v0.2.36: new combatants now carry their init bonus (apply section 6, field 9); the
#          followup `!i add` uses it as the modifier ("!i add <bonus> name") instead of
#          a hardcoded 0. Field absent (older BS export) -> defaults to 0, unchanged.
# v0.2.35: applied-summary now counts SRD monster-adds ("N monster(s)") so the embed no
#          longer says "No changes" when only monsters were added. Counts emitted `!i madd`
#          followups (post-dedupe), parallel to the existing new-combatant count.
# v0.2.34: SRD monster-adds. New apply section 6 (md): one `!i madd <name> (<source>)`
#          per SRD-tagged token, source tag emitted UNQUOTED so Avrae reads it as a
#          source filter (quoting it triggers the disambiguation prompt). Placement note
#          folds in from the matching move entry by name; dedupe + nc_names skip mirror
#          the new-combatant path. Source travels as an alnum code mapped to the literal
#          tag in SRC (free SRD set = "brlegacy" -> "(BR; legacy)").
# v0.2.33: export embed copy - "Click to edit current map in BattleScry" link is now an H1
#          header (bigger), and the How to Use steps renumbered to #1:..#4: with step 1
#          noting the link opens in a new window (desktop only).
# v0.2.32: new combatants added via apply are now created already-placed - their
#          Location/Size/Color (from the move section) are folded into the `!i add -note`,
#          and they are skipped in the move pass. Fixes "shows in init but not on the map".
# v0.2.31: replaced 5 `del X[key]` statements with X.pop(key) - Avrae Draconic forbids the
#          `del` statement (it raised FeatureNotAvailable on overlay/saved-item removal).
# Round-trip data layer between BS (battlescry.com) and Avrae/OTFBM.
# Storage uvars: mapTokens, mapBackgrounds, mapBattles, bscry_tokenLabels (all JSON).
# Modes: (none)=export, apply=write changes, loadmap=replay saved map, loadbattle=replay saved battle.
# ============================================================
c = combat()
args = &ARGS&

# Defensive: strip accidentally-pasted `!bscry <mode>` prefix from args.
# Common typo: user types `!bscry apply ` then pastes BS's full export (which also starts
# with `!bscry apply`), yielding args=["apply", "!bscry", "apply", "<data>"]. We detect
# the doubled `mode + bscry + mode` pattern at the start and squash it back to `mode + <data>`.
_modes = ["apply", "loadmap", "loadbattle"]
while len(args) >= 3 and str(args[0]) in _modes and str(args[1]).lower() in ["!bscry", "bscry"] and str(args[2]) == str(args[0]):
    args = [args[0]] + args[3:]

# ============================================================
# Helpers
# ============================================================
def get_field(txt, name):
    label = name + ": "
    i = txt.find(label)
    if i < 0:
        return ""
    start = i + len(label)
    j_tilde = txt.find(" ~", start)
    j_quote = txt.find("'", start)
    candidates = []
    if j_tilde > start:
        candidates.append(j_tilde)
    if j_quote > start:
        candidates.append(j_quote)
    if not candidates:
        return txt[start:].strip()
    return txt[start:min(candidates)].strip()

def parse_note(note_str):
    flds = {}
    order = []
    if not note_str:
        return flds, order
    for fld in note_str.lstrip("# ").split(" | "):
        fld = fld.strip()
        ci = fld.find(": ")
        if ci > -1:
            k = fld[:ci].strip()
            v = fld[ci+2:].strip()
            if k not in flds:
                order.append(k)
            flds[k] = v
    return flds, order

def build_note(flds, order):
    p = []
    for k in order:
        if k in flds and flds[k] != "":
            p.append(k + ": " + flds[k])
    return " | ".join(p)

def parse_hash_kv(hstr):
    d = {}
    if not hstr:
        return d
    for pair in hstr.split("&"):
        if "=" in pair:
            ei = pair.find("=")
            d[pair[:ei]] = pair[ei+1:]
    return d

def parse_set(s, sep):
    out = set()
    if s:
        for x in s.split(sep):
            x = x.strip()
            if x:
                out.add(x)
    return out

def merge_set(local, base, remote):
    # Three-way merge for sets: start from REMOTE, apply DM diffs.
    # No conflicts reported - set additions are inherently mergeable.
    result = set(remote)
    for x in local:
        if x not in base:
            result.add(x)
    for x in base:
        if x not in local:
            result.discard(x)
    return result

def merge_scalar(local, base, remote, name, desc_tmpl, conflicts):
    # Three-way merge for scalars. Returns merged value. Logs conflict if both changed.
    if not local:
        return remote
    if local == base:
        return remote
    if remote == base:
        return local
    if local == remote:
        return local
    # Conflict - server wins
    conflicts.append((name, desc_tmpl))
    return remote

# Size and color display name maps (for note field formatting)
SZ_NAMES = {"t":"T (Tiny)","s":"S (Small)","m":"M (Medium)","l":"L (Large)","h":"H (Huge)","g":"G (Gargantuan)"}
CL_NAMES = {"r":"r (red)","b":"b (blue)","g":"g (green)","y":"y (yellow)","pk":"pk (pink)","p":"p (purple)","c":"c (cyan)","bn":"bn (brown)","o":"o (orange)","w":"w (white)","bk":"bk (black)"}
# Monster-add source codes -> literal Avrae source tags (emitted UNQUOTED after the name).
# Free SRD set is uniformly "(BR; legacy)". The literal tag lives here, not in the data,
# so a future label change is a one-line fix and the semicolon never hits a delimiter.
SRC = {"brlegacy": "(BR; legacy)", "mm2024": "(MM-2024)", "mmlegacy": "(MM; legacy)"}

def place_note_from_mvp(mvp):
    # Build the OTFBM placement note (Location/Size/Color/Height/Token) from a move entry
    # list (name|coord|size|color|height|token). Mirrors the new-combatant placement fold
    # so a monster-add lands already-positioned via its `!i madd -note`.
    if not mvp:
        return ""
    flds = {}
    order = []
    _coord = mvp[1].strip() if len(mvp) > 1 else ""
    _size = (mvp[2].strip() if len(mvp) > 2 else "").lower()
    _color = (mvp[3].strip() if len(mvp) > 3 else "").lower()
    _height = mvp[4].strip() if len(mvp) > 4 else ""
    _token = mvp[5].strip() if len(mvp) > 5 else ""
    if _coord:
        flds["Location"] = _coord
        order.append("Location")
    if _size:
        flds["Size"] = SZ_NAMES.get(_size, _size.upper())
        order.append("Size")
    if _color:
        flds["Color"] = CL_NAMES.get(_color, _color)
        order.append("Color")
    if _height and _height != "0":
        flds["Height"] = _height + " ft."
        order.append("Height")
    if _token:
        flds["Token"] = _token
        order.append("Token")
    return build_note(flds, order)

# ============================================================
# Argument parsing
# ============================================================
mode = args[0] if len(args) > 0 else ""
is_apply = mode == "apply"
is_loadmap = mode == "loadmap"
is_loadbattle = mode == "loadbattle"
loadmap_name = ""
if is_loadmap and len(args) > 1:
    # Join remaining args to support unquoted multi-word names: `!bscry loadmap dungeon level 1`
    loadmap_name = " ".join(args[1:]).strip()
loadbattle_name = ""
if is_loadbattle and len(args) > 1:
    loadbattle_name = " ".join(args[1:]).strip()
secret = False
data_idx = 1

if is_apply:
    if len(args) > 1 and args[1] == "-h":
        secret = True
        data_idx = 2

# Apply-mode results
apply_status_parts = []
conflicts = []
apply_ok = is_apply
loadmap_status = ""
loadbattle_status = ""

# ============================================================
# AUTO-BOOTSTRAP - if no combat, or combat exists but no host combatant, emit a multiline block
# that initializes the missing pieces then re-invokes the original command. Avrae processes each
# line of the returned string as a separate command (multiline adds 1s delays between them).
# ============================================================
def _rerun_cmd():
    # Reconstruct the original invocation string for the post-bootstrap follow-up embed.
    if is_apply:
        s = "!bscry apply"
        if secret:
            s += " -h"
        if len(args) > data_idx:
            s += " " + args[data_idx]
        return s
    if is_loadmap:
        return "!bscry loadmap " + loadmap_name
    if is_loadbattle:
        return "!bscry loadbattle " + loadbattle_name
    return "!bscry"

def _bootstrap_simple_embed():
    # Seamless path for bare `!bscry` (no apply/loadmap/loadbattle args) with no combat.
    # Build a BS link with saved tokens/maps/battles in the hash so the sidebar populates.
    # No combat state yet (DM is being added by multiline above us) so no map state encoded.
    hash_parts = []
    try:
        _mt = load_json(get_uvar("mapTokens") or "{}")
        if _mt:
            _ents = [str(k).replace(" ", "%20") + ":" + str(v) for k, v in _mt.items()]
            hash_parts.append("st=" + ";".join(_ents))
    except:
        pass
    try:
        _mb = load_json(get_uvar("mapBackgrounds") or "{}")
        if _mb:
            _names = [str(k).replace(" ", "%20") for k in _mb.keys()]
            hash_parts.append("sm=" + ";".join(_names))
    except:
        pass
    try:
        _mbat = load_json(get_uvar("mapBattles") or "{}")
        if _mbat:
            _names = [str(k).replace(" ", "%20") for k in _mbat.keys()]
            hash_parts.append("sb=" + ";".join(_names))
    except:
        pass
    # v0.2.44: combat already has combatants but no host yet - list them so the editor is not empty.
    try:
        if c is not None:
            _np = []
            _ip = []
            _cs = []
            _ig = {}
            for _cb in c.combatants:
                _n = str(_cb.name)
                if _n and _n != "DM" and ";" not in _n and "|" not in _n:
                    _e = _n.replace(" ", "%20")
                    _np.append(_e)
                    _ip.append(_e + ":" + str(_cb.init))
                    _hp = _cb.hp
                    _mx = _cb.max_hp
                    _acv = _cb.ac
                    _hd = "1" if _cb.is_hidden else ""
                    if _hp is not None or _mx is not None or _acv is not None or _hd:
                        _cs.append(_e + ":" + (str(_hp) if _hp is not None else "") + ":" + (str(_mx) if _mx is not None else "") + ":" + (str(_acv) if _acv is not None else "") + ":" + _hd)
                    _g = _cb.group
                    if _g:
                        _gk = str(_g).replace(" ", "%20")
                        if _gk not in _ig:
                            _ig[_gk] = []
                        _ig[_gk].append(_e)
            if _np:
                hash_parts.append("np=" + ";".join(_np))
                hash_parts.append("ip=" + ";".join(_ip))
            if _cs:
                hash_parts.append("cs=" + ";".join(_cs))
            if _ig:
                hash_parts.append("ig=" + ";".join([k + ":" + ",".join(v) for k, v in _ig.items()]))
    except:
        pass
    try:
        hash_parts.append("ch=" + str(ctx.channel.id))
    except:
        pass
    _bs_url = "https://www.battlescry.com/"
    if hash_parts:
        _bs_url += "#" + "&".join(hash_parts)
    return ('embed -title "\u2728 BattleScry - Combat Ready" '
            '-desc "Combat bootstrapped with a DM combatant. [Click here to open BattleScry](' + _bs_url + ')" '
            '-color 0xf59e0b -footer "BattleScry v0.2.48"')

def _bootstrap_followup_with_cmd():
    # Two-paste path for apply/loadmap/loadbattle with no combat.
    # User's clipboard still has the original command they just pasted - tell them to paste it again.
    # No need to embed the command itself; they can recover it from clipboard or scrollback.
    return ('embed -title "\u2705 BattleScry - Combat Ready" '
            '-desc "Combat bootstrapped with a DM combatant. Paste your command again to continue." -color 0x22c55e')

def _bootstrap_block(prefix_lines, simple):
    # prefix_lines: list of bootstrap commands ('!i begin', '!i add 0 DM -p 50') or just ['!i add 0 DM -p 50']
    # simple: True for bare !bscry (seamless), False for apply/loadmap/loadbattle (two-paste)
    body = _bootstrap_simple_embed() if simple else _bootstrap_followup_with_cmd()
    return "multiline\n" + "\n".join(prefix_lines) + "\n!" + body

# Per-user, per-combat key for the merge BASE (see v0.2.43 note).
_base_key = "bscry_load"
try:
    _base_key = "bscry_load_" + str(ctx.author.id)
except:
    pass

# Anything other than a bare `!bscry` or a known mode is a help request or a typo. Answer it here,
# before the bootstrap below, so `!bscry help` never starts a combat as a side effect.
if mode and not (is_apply or is_loadmap or is_loadbattle):
    return ('embed -title "BattleScry - Help" '
            '-desc "`!bscry` - get a link to edit this channel\'s battle map in your browser.\n'
            '`!bscry apply <data>` - paste the command BattleScry copies for you to apply your changes.\n'
            '`!bscry loadmap <name>` - load one of your saved maps.\n'
            '`!bscry loadbattle <name>` - restore a saved battle.\n\n'
            'Run `!bscry` with nothing after it to start. If no combat is running it starts one and adds a DM combatant to hold the map." '
            '-color 0xf59e0b -footer "BattleScry v0.2.48"')

if c is None:
    # No active combat - bootstrap combat + DM combatant in one multiline.
    # First line has no `!` prefix - Avrae auto-prepends it when substituting alias output
    # into the user's message position (matches how text aliases like `!riftbegin` work).
    return _bootstrap_block(["!i begin", "!i add 0 DM -p 50"], not (is_apply or is_loadmap or is_loadbattle))

# Resolve the host combatant that carries the map state. The durable signal is the `map`
# EFFECT on the combatant, not its name: a user can rename the host in Avrae after the map is
# attached, and the effect stays put. Fall back to the DM/Map/Lair name convention for the
# first-ever attach (before any map effect exists) and for bootstrap. Strict name match so
# "Lair Actions" never picks up "Lair".
#
# Detect via get_effect(), NOT by scanning .attacks. Avrae memoises SimpleCombatant.attacks on
# first access per wrapper and add_effect() never clears it, so scanning .attacks here would
# freeze a pre-write snapshot on the long-lived c.combatants wrappers. Croebh's maplib reads
# those same wrappers (load_data() scans combat().combatants[].attacks), so it would then render
# a missing or stale preview. get_effect() reads through to the combatant and memoises nothing.
def find_map_host():
    for _cb in c.combatants:
        try:
            if _cb.get_effect("map", True):
                return _cb
        except:
            pass
    # No map attached yet. If an earlier run recorded which combatant is the host, use it, so a host
    # renamed before the first map is attached is still found instead of a second DM being added.
    try:
        _hid = c.get_metadata("bscry_host")
        if _hid:
            for _cb in c.combatants:
                if str(_cb.id) == str(_hid):
                    return _cb
    except:
        pass
    for _nm in ["DM", "Map", "Lair"]:
        _h = c.get_combatant(_nm, True)
        if _h:
            return _h
    return None

# Read the `map` effect text WITHOUT memoising .attacks on a c.combatants wrapper.
# SimpleCombat.get_combatant() constructs a brand new SimpleCombatant on every call, and the
# .attacks memo is per wrapper, so a throwaway wrapper absorbs the snapshot and the long-lived
# one stays clean for maplib to populate after the write. Falls back to the passed host if the
# name lookup misses (renamed mid-run, or a name Avrae cannot match).
def map_text_of(host):
    if host is None:
        return ""
    _p = c.get_combatant(host.name, True) or host
    try:
        for _atk in _p.attacks:
            if _atk.name == "map":
                try:
                    return _atk.raw.automation[-1].text or ""
                except:
                    return ""
    except:
        pass
    return ""

# Pre-check for a host combatant (see find_map_host above).
_host_check = find_map_host()
if _host_check is None:
    # Combat is active but no DM/Map/Lair - just add a DM combatant.
    return _bootstrap_block(["!i add 0 DM -p 50"], not (is_apply or is_loadmap or is_loadbattle))
# Remember the host by id so a later rename cannot orphan it (read back in find_map_host).
try:
    c.set_metadata("bscry_host", str(_host_check.id))
except:
    pass

# ============================================================
# APPLY PATH - three-way merge + writes
# ============================================================
if is_apply:
    raw = args[data_idx] if len(args) > data_idx else ""
    raw = raw.replace("%7C", "|").replace("%7B", "{").replace("%7D", "}").replace("%20", " ")
    sections = raw.split("::")
    mv_str = sections[0] if len(sections) > 0 else ""
    nt_str = sections[1] if len(sections) > 1 else ""
    ef_str = sections[2] if len(sections) > 2 else ""
    uv_str = sections[3] if len(sections) > 3 else ""
    # Section 5: free-floating overlay shortcodes (no -t target) - rendered inline in the response
    # embed's -image URL only. Not persisted to combat state. ";"-separated OTFBM shortcodes like
    # "c20rG12;t30bA5E5". The alias appends them as "*<sc>" path segments to map_img.
    ff_str = sections[4] if len(sections) > 4 else ""
    # Section 6: new combatants added via BS's Add Combatant form. Format:
    # name|init|ac|hp|hide|note|color|size;next;... Empty fields are valid (no value set).
    # Alias runs `!i add 0 name -p init -ac N -hp N -note "..."` for each, plus `-h` toggle if hidden.
    # New combatants must be processed BEFORE token moves so subsequent ops can reference them.
    nc_str = sections[5] if len(sections) > 5 else ""
    # Section 7: SRD monster-adds. Format per entry (`;`-separated, `|`-fielded):
    #   combatantName|srdName|sourceCode|init|group|hp|ac   (only combatantName + srdName required)
    # Emits one `!i madd <srdName> <tag> -name "..." [...] -note "..."` per entry. Placement is
    # folded in from the matching mv_str entry by name, identical to the nc path.
    md_str = sections[6] if len(sections) > 6 else ""
    # Section 8: edits to combatants already in Avrae (ed). Parsed below, just after the md adds.
    ed_str = sections[7] if len(sections) > 7 else ""
    # Section 9: standalone flag (sa). "1" means the BattleScry session was opened directly at
    # battlescry.com rather than through a !bscry link, so it never observed Avrae's map and holds
    # no meaningful BASE - its map fields are a DECLARATION of the map it wants, not a diff.
    # Absent or "" from BS builds older than v0.1.304 -> normal three-way merge, unchanged.
    sa_str = sections[8] if len(sections) > 8 else ""
    _standalone = sa_str.strip() == "1"

    # Index the move entries by name so a brand-new combatant can be created already-placed:
    # its Location/Size/Color (from mv_str) are baked into the `!i add -note` below. Without this,
    # the move pass would run before the followup `!i add` exists and the token would never get a
    # Location note - so it shows in initiative but not on the map.
    mv_by_name = {}
    if mv_str:
        for _e in mv_str.split(";"):
            _e = _e.strip()
            if not _e or "|" not in _e:
                continue
            _p = _e.split("|")
            if _p[0]:
                mv_by_name[_p[0]] = _p
    nc_names = set()

    # Parse new combatant entries into `!i add` followup commands. Emitted via multiline output
    # at the end of the apply so they run before the response embed. Format per entry:
    # name|init|ac|hp|hide|note|color|size (only `name` required; empty fields skip the flag).
    # Placement (coord/size/color) comes from the matching mv_str entry and is folded into -note.
    nc_followup_cmds = []
    if nc_str:
        for entry in nc_str.split(";"):
            entry = entry.strip()
            if not entry or "|" not in entry:
                continue
            fields = entry.split("|")
            nm = fields[0].strip()
            if not nm:
                continue
            # Skip if combatant already exists - avoids duplicate-add errors on re-paste of apply
            if c.get_combatant(nm, True):
                continue
            nc_names.add(nm)
            init_v = fields[1].strip() if len(fields) > 1 else ""
            ac_v = fields[2].strip() if len(fields) > 2 else ""
            hp_v = fields[3].strip() if len(fields) > 3 else ""
            hide_v = fields[4].strip() if len(fields) > 4 else ""
            note_v = fields[5].strip() if len(fields) > 5 else ""
            ib_v = fields[8].strip() if len(fields) > 8 else ""
            # Build the placement note (Location/Size/Color/Height/Token) from this combatant's
            # mv_str entry, so the new combatant is created already on the map at the right cell.
            place_flds = {}
            place_order = []
            mvp = mv_by_name.get(nm)
            if mvp:
                _coord = mvp[1].strip() if len(mvp) > 1 else ""
                _size = (mvp[2].strip() if len(mvp) > 2 else "").lower()
                _color = (mvp[3].strip() if len(mvp) > 3 else "").lower()
                _height = mvp[4].strip() if len(mvp) > 4 else ""
                _token = mvp[5].strip() if len(mvp) > 5 else ""
                if _coord:
                    place_flds["Location"] = _coord
                    place_order.append("Location")
                if _size:
                    place_flds["Size"] = SZ_NAMES.get(_size, _size.upper())
                    place_order.append("Size")
                if _color:
                    place_flds["Color"] = CL_NAMES.get(_color, _color)
                    place_order.append("Color")
                if _height and _height != "0":
                    place_flds["Height"] = _height + " ft."
                    place_order.append("Height")
                if _token:
                    place_flds["Token"] = _token
                    place_order.append("Token")
            place_note = build_note(place_flds, place_order)
            # Combine placement fields with any free-text note from the Add Combatant form.
            final_note = place_note
            if note_v:
                final_note = (place_note + " | " + note_v) if place_note else note_v
            # Build !i add command - quoting name only if it has spaces (Avrae quirk)
            nm_arg = '"' + nm + '"' if " " in nm else nm
            cmd = "!i add " + (ib_v if ib_v else "0") + " " + nm_arg
            if init_v:
                cmd += " -p " + init_v
            if ac_v:
                cmd += " -ac " + ac_v
            if hp_v:
                cmd += " -hp " + hp_v + " -max " + hp_v
            if final_note:
                # Escape any embedded quotes in the note
                cmd += ' -note "' + final_note.replace('"', "'") + '"'
            nc_followup_cmds.append(cmd)
            # Hidden toggle is a separate command
            if hide_v == "1":
                nc_followup_cmds.append("!i opt " + nm_arg + " -h")

    # --- SRD monster-adds (md_str): one `!i madd` per SRD-tagged token. ----------------
    # srdName + source tag are emitted UNQUOTED (Avrae reads the parenthetical as a source
    # filter only when bare; quoting it triggers the disambiguation prompt). The -name and
    # -note values are quoted. Placement note is folded in from the matching mv_str entry.
    # Dedupe by existing combatant (madd does not self-dedupe) and add to nc_names so the
    # move pass skips them this run (they are created already-placed via the madd -note).
    if md_str:
        for m_entry in md_str.split(";"):
            m_entry = m_entry.strip()
            if not m_entry or "|" not in m_entry:
                continue
            mf = m_entry.split("|")
            m_cn = mf[0].strip()
            m_srd = mf[1].strip() if len(mf) > 1 else ""
            if not m_cn or not m_srd:
                continue
            if c.get_combatant(m_cn, True):
                continue
            nc_names.add(m_cn)
            m_src = mf[2].strip() if len(mf) > 2 else ""
            m_init = mf[3].strip() if len(mf) > 3 else ""
            m_group = mf[4].strip() if len(mf) > 4 else ""
            m_hp = mf[5].strip() if len(mf) > 5 else ""
            m_ac = mf[6].strip() if len(mf) > 6 else ""
            m_tag = SRC.get(m_src, "(BR; legacy)")
            m_note = place_note_from_mvp(mv_by_name.get(m_cn))
            mcmd = "!i madd " + m_srd + " " + m_tag + ' -name "' + m_cn + '"'
            if m_init:
                mcmd += " -p " + m_init
            if m_group:
                mcmd += " -group " + m_group
            if m_hp:
                mcmd += " -hp " + m_hp
            if m_ac:
                mcmd += " -ac " + m_ac
            if m_note:
                mcmd += ' -note "' + m_note.replace('"', "'") + '"'
            nc_followup_cmds.append(mcmd)

    # --- Section 8: replay edits to existing combatants via `!i opt` ----------------------
    # BS sends name|ac|hpCur|hpMax|init|group with only the changed fields populated (empty = no
    # change). Emit one `!i opt "name"` per entry carrying just the changed flags. These ride the
    # same followup list as the new-combatant adds and run after them; they target combatants that
    # already exist in Avrae's initiative. %20 in name/group decodes back to a space.
    ed_updated = 0
    if ed_str:
        for entry in ed_str.split(";"):
            entry = entry.strip()
            if not entry or "|" not in entry:
                continue
            ef = entry.split("|")
            e_name = ef[0].replace("%20", " ").strip()
            if not e_name:
                continue
            e_ac = ef[1].strip() if len(ef) > 1 else ""
            e_hpcur = ef[2].strip() if len(ef) > 2 else ""
            e_hpmax = ef[3].strip() if len(ef) > 3 else ""
            e_init = ef[4].strip() if len(ef) > 4 else ""
            e_group = ef[5].replace("%20", " ").strip() if len(ef) > 5 else ""
            e_arg = '"' + e_name + '"' if " " in e_name else e_name
            opt = "!i opt " + e_arg
            changed = False
            if e_ac:
                opt += " -ac " + e_ac
                changed = True
            if e_hpcur:
                opt += " -hp " + e_hpcur
                changed = True
            if e_hpmax:
                opt += " -max " + e_hpmax
                changed = True
            if e_init:
                opt += " -p " + e_init
                changed = True
            if e_group:
                opt += ' -group "' + e_group + '"'
                changed = True
            if changed:
                nc_followup_cmds.append(opt)
                ed_updated += 1

    # --- Read BASE from uvar (set during last !bscry) ---
    base_hash_str = ""
    try:
        base_hash_str = c.get_metadata(_base_key) or ""
    except:
        base_hash_str = ""
    _base_from_meta = True if base_hash_str else False
    if not base_hash_str:
        base_hash_str = get_uvar("bscry_load") or ""
    if base_hash_str:
        base_hash_str = base_hash_str.replace("%7C", "|").replace("%7B", "{").replace("%7D", "}").replace("%20", " ")
    base = parse_hash_kv(base_hash_str)

    # Parse BASE tokens - name -> {coord, size, color, height, token}
    base_toks = {}
    if base.get("t"):
        for entry in base["t"].split(";"):
            if not entry:
                continue
            parts = entry.split("|")
            if len(parts) >= 2:
                nm = parts[0].strip()
                if nm:
                    base_toks[nm] = {
                        "coord": parts[1].strip() if len(parts) > 1 else "",
                        "size": parts[2].strip() if len(parts) > 2 else "",
                        "color": parts[3].strip() if len(parts) > 3 else "",
                        "height": parts[4].strip() if len(parts) > 4 else "",
                        "token": parts[5].strip() if len(parts) > 5 else ""
                    }

    base_walls = parse_set(base.get("w", ""), ",")
    base_fow = parse_set(base.get("fw", ""), ",")
    base_objs = parse_set(base.get("ob", ""), ";")
    base_grid = base.get("g", "")
    base_bg = base.get("bg", "")
    base_opts = base.get("o", "")
    base_view = base.get("vw", "")

    # --- Read REMOTE map effect (current Discord/Avrae state) ---
    map_host = find_map_host()

    remote_walls = set()
    remote_fow = set()
    remote_objs = set()
    remote_grid = ""
    remote_bg = ""
    remote_opts = ""
    remote_view = ""

    if map_host:
        cur_text = map_text_of(map_host)
        if cur_text:
            remote_walls = parse_set(get_field(cur_text, "Walls"), ", ")
            remote_fow = parse_set(get_field(cur_text, "FOW"), ", ")
            remote_objs = parse_set(get_field(cur_text, "Objects"), "/")
            remote_grid = get_field(cur_text, "Size")
            remote_bg = get_field(cur_text, "Background")
            remote_opts = get_field(cur_text, "Options")
            remote_view = get_field(cur_text, "View")

    # Detect fresh combat: if the host has no map effect at all, bscry_load is stale (from a
    # previous session/combat). Clear BASE so the three-way merge degenerates to "no conflicts,
    # local wins" - which is correct semantics for an apply into a freshly-bootstrapped combat.
    _fresh_combat = not (remote_grid or remote_bg or remote_opts or remote_view or remote_walls or remote_fow or remote_objs)
    # A standalone session (section 9) has no BASE for the same reason a fresh combat does not:
    # nothing BattleScry holds describes Avrae's current map, so bscry_load is not its baseline.
    # Clearing BASE also makes merge_set additive (remote | local), so a standalone export adds its
    # walls/FOW/objects without deleting anything already on the map.
    # v0.2.46: BASE now lives in this combat's metadata, so it is only stale when it came from the
    # old uvar fallback. A combat with tokens placed but no map effect yet keeps its BASE.
    _no_base = (_fresh_combat and not _base_from_meta) or _standalone
    if _no_base:
        base_toks = {}
        base_walls = set()
        base_fow = set()
        base_objs = set()
        base_grid = ""
        base_bg = ""
        base_opts = ""
        base_view = ""

    # --- Parse LOCAL (BattleScry's intended state) from ef_str ---
    local_walls = parse_set(get_field(ef_str, "Walls"), ", ")
    local_fow = parse_set(get_field(ef_str, "FOW"), ", ")
    local_objs = parse_set(get_field(ef_str, "Objects"), "/")
    local_grid = get_field(ef_str, "Size")
    local_bg = get_field(ef_str, "Background")
    local_opts = get_field(ef_str, "Options")
    local_view = get_field(ef_str, "View")

    # If BS sent empty ef_str, it's signaling "no changes to the map effect" (not "delete all").
    # Mirror remote into local so the merge becomes a no-op (no writes, no false-conflicts, nothing removed).
    if not ef_str.strip():
        local_walls = set(remote_walls)
        local_fow = set(remote_fow)
        local_objs = set(remote_objs)
        local_grid = remote_grid
        local_bg = remote_bg
        local_opts = remote_opts
        local_view = remote_view

    # --- Merge map sets (walls, FOW, objects) ---
    merged_walls = merge_set(local_walls, base_walls, remote_walls)
    merged_fow = merge_set(local_fow, base_fow, remote_fow)
    merged_objs = merge_set(local_objs, base_objs, remote_objs)

    # Set-change detection for status (DM additions/removals that survived merge)
    dm_walls_added = local_walls - base_walls
    dm_walls_removed = base_walls - local_walls
    srv_walls_added = remote_walls - base_walls
    dm_fow_added = local_fow - base_fow
    dm_fow_removed = base_fow - local_fow
    dm_objs_added = local_objs - base_objs
    dm_objs_removed = base_objs - local_objs

    # --- Merge map scalars (size, bg, opts, view) ---
    if _standalone:
        # No BASE to merge against, so BattleScry's map fields are taken as given. Anything BS left
        # empty falls back to the current map rather than blanking it. No conflicts are logged,
        # because there is no baseline that could meaningfully disagree - the three-way merge would
        # otherwise compare against an unrelated earlier session and discard the user's map.
        final_grid = local_grid if local_grid else remote_grid
        final_bg = local_bg if local_bg else remote_bg
        final_opts = local_opts if local_opts else remote_opts
        final_view = local_view if local_view else remote_view
    else:
        final_grid = merge_scalar(local_grid, base_grid, remote_grid, "Map size",
            "Map size (you edited " + (base_grid or "?") + "→" + (local_grid or "?") + ", but it's now " + (remote_grid or "?") + ")",
            conflicts)
        final_bg = merge_scalar(local_bg, base_bg, remote_bg, "Background",
            "Background image changed since you loaded",
            conflicts)
        final_opts = merge_scalar(local_opts, base_opts, remote_opts, "Map options",
            "Map options changed since you loaded",
            conflicts)
        final_view = merge_scalar(local_view, base_view, remote_view, "View",
            "View settings changed since you loaded",
            conflicts)

    # --- Detect set conflicts: walls/FOW/objects DM removed but server modified ---
    # (Currently captured implicitly via merge_set - server wins. We can also surface as info.)
    # Items in (BASE - LOCAL) that REMOTE also has are "DM removed, but server also touched":
    # since we have no IDs, we treat these as DM-only removals (apply removal). No conflict.
    # Items in (BASE - REMOTE) that LOCAL still has are "server removed, DM kept" → conflict.
    walls_srv_removed_dm_kept = (base_walls - remote_walls) & local_walls
    for w in walls_srv_removed_dm_kept:
        conflicts.append(("Walls", "Walls: " + w + " was removed from the map since you loaded"))
    fow_srv_removed_dm_kept = (base_fow - remote_fow) & local_fow
    for f in fow_srv_removed_dm_kept:
        conflicts.append(("FOW", "FOW: " + f + " was removed from the map since you loaded"))
    objs_srv_removed_dm_kept = (base_objs - remote_objs) & local_objs
    for o in objs_srv_removed_dm_kept:
        conflicts.append(("Objects", "Object " + o + " was removed from the map since you loaded"))

    # --- Build merged map effect text ---
    ep = []
    if final_grid:
        ep.append("Size: " + final_grid)
    if final_bg:
        ep.append("Background: " + final_bg)
    if final_opts:
        ep.append("Options: " + final_opts)
    if merged_walls:
        ep.append("Walls: " + ", ".join(list(merged_walls)))
    if merged_objs:
        ep.append("Objects: " + "/".join(list(merged_objs)))
    if final_view:
        ep.append("View: " + final_view)
    if merged_fow:
        ep.append("FOW: " + ", ".join(list(merged_fow)))
    new_ef_str = " ~ ".join(ep)

    # --- Write merged map effect ---
    map_did_change = (merged_walls != remote_walls) or (merged_fow != remote_fow) or (merged_objs != remote_objs) or (final_grid != remote_grid) or (final_bg != remote_bg) or (final_opts != remote_opts) or (final_view != remote_view)
    if new_ef_str and map_host and map_did_change:
        try:
            if map_host.get_effect("map"):
                map_host.remove_effect("map")
        except:
            pass
        try:
            map_host.add_effect("map", attacks=[{"attack":{"name":"map","automation":[{"type":"text","text":new_ef_str}],"_v":2}}])
        except Exception as exc:
            conflicts.append(("Map effect", "Failed to write map effect: " + str(exc)))

    # --- Three-way merge tokens (mv_str) ---
    tokens_updated = 0
    handled_names = set()

    if mv_str:
        for entry in mv_str.split(";"):
            entry = entry.strip()
            if not entry or "|" not in entry:
                continue
            parts = entry.split("|")
            name = parts[0]
            if not name:
                continue
            # New combatants are created already-placed via their followup `!i add -note`, and they
            # don't exist during this run yet - skip them here to avoid a false "not in combat" conflict.
            if name in nc_names:
                continue
            handled_names.add(name)
            local_coord = parts[1].strip() if len(parts) > 1 else ""
            local_size = (parts[2].strip() if len(parts) > 2 else "").lower()
            local_color = (parts[3].strip() if len(parts) > 3 else "").lower()
            local_height = parts[4].strip() if len(parts) > 4 else ""
            local_token = parts[5].strip() if len(parts) > 5 else ""

            cmb = c.get_combatant(name)
            if not cmb:
                conflicts.append(("token", name + " is no longer in combat - change skipped"))
                continue

            note = str(cmb.note) if cmb.note else ""
            flds, order = parse_note(note)

            base_t = base_toks.get(name, {})
            base_coord = base_t.get("coord", "")
            base_size = (base_t.get("size", "") or "").lower()
            base_color = (base_t.get("color", "") or "").lower()
            base_height = base_t.get("height", "") or ""
            base_token = base_t.get("token", "") or ""

            remote_coord = flds.get("Location", "")
            remote_size_d = flds.get("Size", "")
            remote_size = remote_size_d[:1].lower() if remote_size_d else ""
            remote_color_d = flds.get("Color", "")
            remote_color = remote_color_d.split(" ")[0].lower() if remote_color_d else ""
            remote_height_d = flds.get("Height", "")
            remote_height = remote_height_d.split(" ")[0] if remote_height_d else ""
            remote_token = flds.get("Token", "")

            tok_changed = False

            # Location merge
            if local_coord:
                if local_coord == base_coord:
                    pass
                elif remote_coord == base_coord or not remote_coord or _no_base:
                    if "Location" not in order:
                        order.insert(0, "Location")
                    flds["Location"] = local_coord
                    tok_changed = True
                elif local_coord == remote_coord:
                    pass
                else:
                    conflicts.append(("token", name + "'s position (you edited " + base_coord + "→" + local_coord + ", but it's now at " + remote_coord + ")"))

            # Size merge
            if local_size:
                if local_size == base_size:
                    pass
                elif remote_size == base_size or not remote_size:
                    flds["Size"] = SZ_NAMES.get(local_size, local_size.upper())
                    if "Size" not in order:
                        order.append("Size")
                    tok_changed = True
                elif local_size == remote_size:
                    pass
                else:
                    conflicts.append(("token", name + "'s size changed externally - yours discarded"))

            # Color merge
            if local_color:
                if local_color == base_color:
                    pass
                elif remote_color == base_color or not remote_color:
                    flds["Color"] = CL_NAMES.get(local_color, local_color)
                    if "Color" not in order:
                        order.append("Color")
                    tok_changed = True
                elif local_color == remote_color:
                    pass
                else:
                    conflicts.append(("token", name + "'s color changed externally - yours discarded"))

            # Height merge
            if local_height and local_height != "0":
                if local_height == base_height:
                    pass
                elif remote_height == base_height or not remote_height:
                    flds["Height"] = local_height + " ft."
                    if "Height" not in order:
                        order.append("Height")
                    tok_changed = True
                elif local_height == remote_height:
                    pass
                else:
                    conflicts.append(("token", name + "'s height changed externally - yours discarded"))

            # Token image merge
            if local_token:
                if local_token == base_token:
                    pass
                elif remote_token == base_token or not remote_token:
                    flds["Token"] = local_token
                    if "Token" not in order:
                        order.append("Token")
                    tok_changed = True
                elif local_token == remote_token:
                    pass
                else:
                    conflicts.append(("token", name + "'s token image changed externally - yours discarded"))

            if tok_changed:
                cmb.set_note(build_note(flds, order))
                tokens_updated += 1

    # --- Overlay-only note updates (nt_str) - merge Overlay/Aim fields into current note ---
    overlays_updated = 0
    if nt_str:
        for entry in nt_str.split(";;"):
            if "~" not in entry:
                continue
            ti = entry.find("~")
            n = entry[:ti].strip()
            new_note_str = entry[ti+1:]
            if n in handled_names:
                # Token was already merged above - also apply overlay fields from this note
                pass
            cmb = c.get_combatant(n) or (map_host if n == "DM" else None)
            if not cmb:
                continue

            cur_note = str(cmb.note) if cmb.note else ""
            cur_flds, cur_order = parse_note(cur_note)
            new_flds, new_order = parse_note(new_note_str)

            # Merge: overlay-related fields come from LOCAL; non-overlay fields preserved from REMOTE.
            # Slots: "Overlay" is slot 0 (unnumbered, OTFBM *), "Overlay1".."Overlay10" are slots 1-10 (OTFBM *1..*10).
            # Matches Croebh's map.alias range(1,11) in line 705. Underlays share the same slot family (leading 'u' in the value).
            ov_keys = ["Overlay", "Overlay1", "Overlay2", "Overlay3", "Overlay4", "Overlay5", "Overlay6", "Overlay7", "Overlay8", "Overlay9", "Overlay10",
                       "Aim", "Aim1", "Aim2", "Aim3", "Aim4", "Aim5", "Aim6", "Aim7", "Aim8", "Aim9", "Aim10"]
            merged = dict(cur_flds)
            merged_order = list(cur_order)
            # Set or replace overlay fields per LOCAL
            for k in ov_keys:
                if k in new_flds and new_flds[k]:
                    if k not in merged_order:
                        merged_order.append(k)
                    merged[k] = new_flds[k]
            # Remove overlay fields LOCAL doesn't have (DM removed them)
            for k in ov_keys:
                if k not in new_flds and k in merged:
                    merged.pop(k)
                    if k in merged_order:
                        merged_order.remove(k)

            new_note_built = build_note(merged, merged_order)
            if new_note_built != cur_note:
                cmb.set_note(new_note_built)
                overlays_updated += 1

    # --- Apply uvar ops (4th section): st+/st-/sm+/sm-/sb+/sb-/tl+/tl-, joined by ;;
    # st: saved tokens (writes to mapTokens, JSON dict {name: shortcode}, lowercased per Croebh convention).
    # sm: saved maps (writes to mapBackgrounds, JSON dict {name: {mapbg, mapsize, mapoptions, walls, objects, view, fow}}, lowercased).
    # sb: saved battles (writes to mapBattles, JSON dict {name: {mapattach: {...}, CombatantName: {...}, ...}}, lowercased name).
    # tl: token label metadata for baked tokens (writes to bscry_tokenLabels JSON {name: {orig, text, size, color, bg, pos}}).
    #     A baked token has BOTH a st+ entry (shortcode in mapTokens) AND a tl+ entry (metadata in bscry_tokenLabels).
    # Names already have underscores decoded to spaces by line 122. All names lowercased on write to mapTokens for !map compatibility.
    saved_tokens_changed = 0
    saved_maps_changed = 0
    saved_battles_changed = 0
    token_labels_changed = 0
    if uv_str:
        # Read current uvars. mapTokens, mapBackgrounds, mapBattles, and bscry_tokenLabels are all JSON dicts.
        cur_mt_raw = get_uvar("mapTokens") or "{}"
        cur_mb_raw = get_uvar("mapBackgrounds") or "{}"
        cur_mbat_raw = get_uvar("mapBattles") or "{}"
        cur_tl_raw = get_uvar("bscry_tokenLabels") or "{}"

        # Parse mapTokens (JSON dict {name: shortcode}). Tolerate malformed JSON by starting fresh.
        try:
            mt_dict = load_json(cur_mt_raw)
            if not mt_dict:
                mt_dict = {}
        except:
            mt_dict = {}

        # Parse mapBackgrounds (JSON dict {name: {mapbg, mapsize, mapoptions, walls, objects, view, fow}}).
        try:
            mb_dict = load_json(cur_mb_raw)
            if not mb_dict:
                mb_dict = {}
        except:
            mb_dict = {}

        # Parse mapBattles (JSON dict {name: {mapattach: {...}, CombatantName: {...}, ...}}).
        try:
            mbat_dict = load_json(cur_mbat_raw)
            if not mbat_dict:
                mbat_dict = {}
        except:
            mbat_dict = {}

        # Parse bscry_tokenLabels (JSON dict {name: {orig, text, size, color, bg, pos}}).
        try:
            tl_dict = load_json(cur_tl_raw)
            if not tl_dict:
                tl_dict = {}
        except:
            tl_dict = {}

        # Apply each op
        for op in uv_str.split(";;"):
            op = op.strip()
            if not op or len(op) < 4:
                continue
            kind = op[:2]
            sign = op[2]
            rest = op[3:].strip()
            if not rest:
                continue
            if kind == "st" and sign == "+":
                if ":" in rest:
                    ci = rest.find(":")
                    name = rest[:ci].strip().lower()  # Croebh convention: mapTokens is lowercased
                    code = rest[ci+1:].strip().lower()
                    if name and code:
                        mt_dict[name] = code
                        saved_tokens_changed += 1
            elif kind == "st" and sign == "-":
                key = rest.lower()
                if key in mt_dict:
                    mt_dict.pop(key)
                    saved_tokens_changed += 1
            elif kind == "sm" and sign == "+":
                # Format: name|mapbg|mapsize|mapoptions|walls|objects|view|fow|thumb (9 fields).
                # walls/objects come in as Croebh-format strings; split into arrays for storage.
                # thumb (field 9) is an OTFBM URL BS computes client-side at save time. Used by BS
                # to preview saved maps before loading. Croebh's `!map -mapload` ignores unknown
                # fields, so adding `thumb` is non-breaking.
                fields = rest.split("|")
                if len(fields) >= 1 and fields[0].strip():
                    name = fields[0].strip().lower()
                    walls_str = fields[4] if len(fields) > 4 else ""
                    objs_str = fields[5] if len(fields) > 5 else ""
                    # Walls are ", "-separated; Objects use "/" in OTFBM but BS hash uses ";"
                    walls_arr = [w.strip() for w in walls_str.split(",") if w.strip()] if walls_str else []
                    objs_arr = [o.strip() for o in objs_str.replace(";", "/").split("/") if o.strip()] if objs_str else []
                    _entry = {
                        "mapbg": fields[1].strip() if len(fields) > 1 else "",
                        "mapsize": fields[2].strip() if len(fields) > 2 else "",
                        "mapoptions": fields[3].strip() if len(fields) > 3 else "",
                        "walls": walls_arr,
                        "objects": objs_arr,
                        "view": fields[6].strip() if len(fields) > 6 else "",
                        "fow": fields[7].strip() if len(fields) > 7 else "",
                    }
                    _thumb = fields[8].strip() if len(fields) > 8 else ""
                    if _thumb:
                        _entry["thumb"] = _thumb
                    mb_dict[name] = _entry
                    saved_maps_changed += 1
            elif kind == "sm" and sign == "-":
                key = rest.lower()
                if key in mb_dict:
                    mb_dict.pop(key)
                    saved_maps_changed += 1
            elif kind == "sb" and sign == "+":
                # Format: sb+<JSON>. The JSON is `{"BattleName": {mapattach: {...}, CombatantName: {...}, ...}}` (one top-level key).
                # Using JSON-as-payload instead of pipe-fields because per-combatant data is variable-length and unbounded-field-count.
                try:
                    entry_dict = load_json(rest)
                    if entry_dict:
                        for name, data in entry_dict.items():
                            key = str(name).strip().lower()
                            if key and data:
                                mbat_dict[key] = data
                                saved_battles_changed += 1
                except:
                    pass
            elif kind == "sb" and sign == "-":
                key = rest.lower()
                if key in mbat_dict:
                    mbat_dict.pop(key)
                    saved_battles_changed += 1
            elif kind == "tl" and sign == "+":
                # Format: name|orig|text|size|color|bg|pos (7 fields). Shortcode lives in mapTokens via paired st+.
                fields = rest.split("|")
                if len(fields) >= 1 and fields[0].strip():
                    name = fields[0].strip().lower()
                    tl_dict[name] = {
                        "orig": fields[1].strip().lower() if len(fields) > 1 else "",
                        "text": fields[2] if len(fields) > 2 else "",
                        "size": fields[3] if len(fields) > 3 else "M",
                        "color": fields[4] if len(fields) > 4 else "w",
                        "bg": fields[5] if len(fields) > 5 else "bk",
                        "pos": fields[6] if len(fields) > 6 else "bc",
                    }
                    token_labels_changed += 1
            elif kind == "tl" and sign == "-":
                key = rest.lower()
                if key in tl_dict:
                    tl_dict.pop(key)
                    token_labels_changed += 1

        # Write back. mapTokens, mapBackgrounds, mapBattles, and bscry_tokenLabels are all JSON.
        new_mt_json = dump_json(mt_dict)
        new_mb_json = dump_json(mb_dict)
        new_mbat_json = dump_json(mbat_dict)
        new_tl_json = dump_json(tl_dict)
        # Soft-warn if any uvar approaches the 9000-char limit.
        if len(new_mt_json) > 8000:
            warns.append("\u26a0 mapTokens uvar approaching size limit (" + str(len(new_mt_json)) + "/9000 chars). Consider deleting unused saved tokens.")
        if len(new_mb_json) > 8000:
            warns.append("\u26a0 mapBackgrounds uvar approaching size limit (" + str(len(new_mb_json)) + "/9000 chars). Consider deleting unused saved maps.")
        if len(new_mbat_json) > 8000:
            warns.append("\u26a0 mapBattles uvar approaching size limit (" + str(len(new_mbat_json)) + "/9000 chars). Consider deleting unused saved battles.")
        if len(new_tl_json) > 8000:
            warns.append("\u26a0 bscry_tokenLabels uvar approaching size limit (" + str(len(new_tl_json)) + "/9000 chars). Consider deleting unused baked tokens.")
        if saved_tokens_changed:
            set_uvar("mapTokens", new_mt_json)
        if saved_maps_changed:
            set_uvar("mapBackgrounds", new_mb_json)
        if saved_battles_changed:
            set_uvar("mapBattles", new_mbat_json)
        if token_labels_changed:
            set_uvar("bscry_tokenLabels", new_tl_json)

    # --- Build apply status parts ---
    if tokens_updated:
        apply_status_parts.append(str(tokens_updated) + " token" + ("s" if tokens_updated != 1 else ""))
    if overlays_updated:
        apply_status_parts.append(str(overlays_updated) + " overlay" + ("s" if overlays_updated != 1 else ""))
    wall_chg = len(dm_walls_added) + len(dm_walls_removed)
    if wall_chg:
        apply_status_parts.append(str(wall_chg) + " wall" + ("s" if wall_chg != 1 else ""))
    fow_chg = len(dm_fow_added) + len(dm_fow_removed)
    if fow_chg:
        apply_status_parts.append(str(fow_chg) + " FOW region" + ("s" if fow_chg != 1 else ""))
    obj_chg = len(dm_objs_added) + len(dm_objs_removed)
    if obj_chg:
        apply_status_parts.append(str(obj_chg) + " object" + ("s" if obj_chg != 1 else ""))
    if saved_tokens_changed:
        apply_status_parts.append(str(saved_tokens_changed) + " saved token" + ("s" if saved_tokens_changed != 1 else ""))
    if saved_maps_changed:
        apply_status_parts.append(str(saved_maps_changed) + " saved map" + ("s" if saved_maps_changed != 1 else ""))
    if saved_battles_changed:
        apply_status_parts.append(str(saved_battles_changed) + " saved battle" + ("s" if saved_battles_changed != 1 else ""))
    if token_labels_changed:
        apply_status_parts.append(str(token_labels_changed) + " baked label" + ("s" if token_labels_changed != 1 else ""))
    # The map effect itself. Without this a standalone export that only swaps the background
    # reports "No changes" even though the map was rewritten, which reads as a silent failure.
    if map_did_change:
        apply_status_parts.append("map")
    # New combatants added via BS's Add Combatant form. Count the followup `!i add` commands
    # we'll emit (each combatant produces 1 add + optionally 1 hide-toggle, so use a name set).
    nc_added = 0
    for _c in nc_followup_cmds:
        if _c.startswith("!i add "):
            nc_added += 1
    if nc_added:
        apply_status_parts.append(str(nc_added) + " new combatant" + ("s" if nc_added != 1 else ""))

    # SRD monsters added via the md section. Count the followup `!i madd` commands we'll emit
    # (one per monster, post-dedupe). `!i madd ` does not match the `!i add ` test above, so the
    # two counts never overlap. A re-paste emits nothing, so this honestly reports 0.
    md_added = 0
    for _c in nc_followup_cmds:
        if _c.startswith("!i madd "):
            md_added += 1
    if md_added:
        apply_status_parts.append(str(md_added) + " monster" + ("s" if md_added != 1 else ""))

    # Existing combatants whose ac/hp/maxhp/init/group BS changed, replayed via `!i opt` (section 8).
    if ed_updated:
        apply_status_parts.append(str(ed_updated) + " updated combatant" + ("s" if ed_updated != 1 else ""))

# ============================================================
# EXPORT PATH / URL BUILDER - reads current state, builds BS URL
# (runs for both !bscry and as the click-link in !bscry apply)
# ============================================================
bg = ""
gs = ""
opts = ""
vw = ""
walls = ""
fow = ""
objs = ""
map_host = find_map_host()

# Loadmap mode: write a saved map's state into the active map effect, then continue with normal flow.
if is_loadmap and loadmap_name:
    if not map_host:
        loadmap_status = "\u26a0 No DM/Map/Lair combatant found to attach the map to. Run `!map -attach <combatant>` first."
    else:
        try:
            mb_raw = get_uvar("mapBackgrounds") or "{}"
            mb_dict = load_json(mb_raw)
            if not mb_dict:
                mb_dict = {}
        except:
            mb_dict = {}
        # Find entry by case-insensitive substring match (matches Croebh's `-mapload` behavior).
        # Tolerant of underscore-vs-space mismatch: BS slugifies "Goblin Lair" to "goblin_lair" but
        # Croebh-saved keys may contain spaces ("goblin lair"). Normalize both sides for the match.
        target_lower = loadmap_name.lower().replace("_", " ")
        found_name = None
        found_entry = None
        for k, v in mb_dict.items():
            k_norm = str(k).lower().replace("_", " ")
            if target_lower in k_norm:
                found_name = k
                found_entry = v
                break
        if not found_entry:
            loadmap_status = "\u26a0 No saved map matching `" + loadmap_name + "` found in mapBackgrounds."
        else:
            # Build a map effect text matching Croebh's format: `Field: value ~ Field: value ~ ...`
            ep = []
            mb = str(found_entry.get("mapbg", "") or "")
            ms = str(found_entry.get("mapsize", "") or "")
            mo = str(found_entry.get("mapoptions", "") or "")
            mv = str(found_entry.get("view", "") or "")
            mw = found_entry.get("walls", []) or []
            mo_objs = found_entry.get("objects", []) or []
            mf = str(found_entry.get("fow", "") or "")
            mj = found_entry.get("json", []) or []
            if mb:
                ep.append("Background: " + mb)
            if ms:
                ep.append("Size: " + ms)
            if mo:
                ep.append("Options: " + mo)
            if mv:
                ep.append("View: " + mv)
            if mw:
                ep.append("Walls: " + ", ".join([str(x) for x in mw]))
            if mo_objs:
                ep.append("Objects: " + "/".join([str(x) for x in mo_objs]))
            if mf:
                ep.append("FOW: " + mf)
            if mj:
                ep.append("Json: " + ", ".join([str(x) for x in mj]))
            new_ef_str = " ~ ".join(ep)
            # Replace the existing map effect with the loaded one.
            try:
                if map_host.get_effect("map"):
                    map_host.remove_effect("map")
            except:
                pass
            try:
                map_host.add_effect("map", attacks=[{"attack":{"name":"map","automation":[{"type":"text","text":new_ef_str}],"_v":2}}])
                loadmap_status = "\u2705 Loaded saved map `" + str(found_name) + "` into the active map."
            except Exception as exc:
                loadmap_status = "\u26a0 Failed to write loaded map: " + str(exc)

# Loadbattle mode: replay a saved battle. Writes the mapattach state into the active map effect AND
# restores per-combatant notes (location, size, color, etc) on each saved combatant still in combat.
# Mirrors Croebh's `!map -loadbattle` behavior: aborts if any saved combatant is missing from active combat.
if is_loadbattle and loadbattle_name:
    if not map_host:
        loadbattle_status = "\u26a0 No DM/Map/Lair combatant found to attach the map to. Run `!map -attach <combatant>` first."
    else:
        try:
            mbat_raw = get_uvar("mapBattles") or "{}"
            mbat_dict = load_json(mbat_raw)
            if not mbat_dict:
                mbat_dict = {}
        except:
            mbat_dict = {}
        # Tolerant of underscore-vs-space mismatch (see loadmap notes).
        target_lower = loadbattle_name.lower().replace("_", " ")
        found_btl_name = None
        found_btl_entry = None
        for k, v in mbat_dict.items():
            k_norm = str(k).lower().replace("_", " ")
            if target_lower in k_norm and v:
                found_btl_name = k
                found_btl_entry = v
                break
        if not found_btl_entry:
            loadbattle_status = "\u26a0 No saved battle matching `" + loadbattle_name + "` found in mapBattles."
        else:
            # Validate all combatants exist (Croebh aborts otherwise to avoid silent half-loads).
            missing = []
            for ck in found_btl_entry.keys():
                if ck == "mapattach":
                    continue
                if not c.get_combatant(str(ck), True):
                    missing.append(str(ck))
            if missing:
                loadbattle_status = "\u26a0 Add the combatant" + ("s " if len(missing) > 1 else " ") + "`" + ", ".join(missing) + "` to load this battle (Croebh's loadbattle behavior)."
            else:
                # Write the mapattach state via the same effect-text format used by loadmap.
                mapattach = found_btl_entry.get("mapattach") or {}
                if mapattach:
                    ep = []
                    mb = str(mapattach.get("mapbg", "") or "")
                    ms = str(mapattach.get("mapsize", "") or "")
                    mo = str(mapattach.get("mapoptions", "") or "")
                    mv = str(mapattach.get("view", "") or "")
                    mw = mapattach.get("walls", []) or []
                    mo_objs = mapattach.get("objects", []) or []
                    mf = str(mapattach.get("fow", "") or "")
                    mj = mapattach.get("json", []) or []
                    if mb:
                        ep.append("Background: " + mb)
                    if ms:
                        ep.append("Size: " + ms)
                    if mo:
                        ep.append("Options: " + mo)
                    if mv:
                        ep.append("View: " + mv)
                    if mw:
                        ep.append("Walls: " + ", ".join([str(x) for x in mw]))
                    if mo_objs:
                        ep.append("Objects: " + "/".join([str(x) for x in mo_objs]))
                    if mf:
                        ep.append("FOW: " + mf)
                    if mj:
                        ep.append("Json: " + ", ".join([str(x) for x in mj]))
                    new_ef_str = " ~ ".join(ep)
                    try:
                        if map_host.get_effect("map"):
                            map_host.remove_effect("map")
                    except:
                        pass
                    try:
                        map_host.add_effect("map", attacks=[{"attack":{"name":"map","automation":[{"type":"text","text":new_ef_str}],"_v":2}}])
                    except Exception as exc:
                        loadbattle_status = "\u26a0 Failed to write loaded battle map: " + str(exc)
                # Restore per-combatant notes from saved fields.
                # Lowercase storage keys ("location", "size", ...) are title-cased to match the BS/Croebh note format ("Location: A5 | Size: M (Medium)").
                restored = 0
                for ck, cv in found_btl_entry.items():
                    if ck == "mapattach":
                        continue
                    if not cv:
                        continue
                    cmb = c.get_combatant(str(ck), True)
                    if not cmb:
                        continue
                    parts = []
                    for fk, fv in cv.items():
                        if fv is None or fv == "":
                            continue
                        key_title = fk[0].upper() + fk[1:] if fk else fk
                        parts.append(key_title + ": " + str(fv))
                    try:
                        cmb.set_note(" | ".join(parts))
                        restored += 1
                    except:
                        pass
                if not loadbattle_status:
                    loadbattle_status = "\u2705 Loaded saved battle `" + str(found_btl_name) + "` (" + str(restored) + " combatant" + ("s" if restored != 1 else "") + " updated)."

if map_host:
    txt = map_text_of(map_host)
    if not txt:
        for e in map_host.effects:
            if e.name == "map" and e.attacks:
                txt = str(e.attacks)
                break
    if txt:
        v = get_field(txt, "Size")
        if v:
            gs = v
        v = get_field(txt, "Background")
        if v:
            bg = v
        v = get_field(txt, "Options")
        if v:
            opts = v
        v = get_field(txt, "View")
        if v:
            vw = v
        v = get_field(txt, "Walls")
        if v:
            walls = v
        v = get_field(txt, "FOW")
        if v:
            fow = v
        v = get_field(txt, "Objects")
        if v:
            objs = v

# Token shortcode map - resolve "name" -> shortcode via mapTokens uvar (Croebh's JSON format).
tkmap = {}
try:
    raw_tkmap = get_uvar("mapTokens") or "{}"
    parsed_tk = load_json(raw_tkmap)
    if parsed_tk:
        for k, v in parsed_tk.items():
            ks = str(k).strip().lower()
            vs = str(v).strip()
            if ks and vs:
                tkmap[ks] = vs
except:
    tkmap = {}

# Tokens, overlays, unplaced, full-notes, init order, init groups
tparts = []
np_parts = []
fn_notes = []
ovs = []
ip_parts = []
cs_parts = []
ig_parts = {}

# v0.2.47: names containing ; or | would break the link format, so they are left out and reported.
bad_names = []
for cmb in c.combatants:
    nm = cmb.name
    if not nm or nm == "DM" or (map_host and nm == map_host.name):
        continue
    if ";" in nm or "|" in nm:
        bad_names.append(nm)
        continue
    note = str(cmb.note) if cmb.note else ""
    flds, order = parse_note(note)
    loc = flds.get("Location", "")
    sz = flds.get("Size", "")
    cl = flds.get("Color", "")
    ht = flds.get("Height", "")
    tk = flds.get("Token", "")
    # Compact size/color codes
    sz_code = sz[:1].lower() if sz else "m"
    cl_code = cl.split(" ")[0].lower() if cl else "b"
    ht_n = ht.split(" ")[0] if ht else "0"
    # Resolve shortcode via tkmap if it's a name reference
    if tk and tk.lower() in tkmap:
        tk = tkmap[tk.lower()]
    # Extract all numbered Overlay/Aim fields ("Overlay" + "Overlay2" + ..., "Aim" + "Aim2" + ...)
    ov_fields = {}
    aim_fields = {}
    for k in flds:
        if k.startswith("Overlay"):
            num = k.replace("Overlay", "")
            ov_fields[num] = flds[k]
        elif k.startswith("Aim"):
            num = k.replace("Aim", "")
            aim_fields[num] = flds[k]
    sn = nm.replace(" ", "%20")
    # Combatant stats (current HP / max HP / AC) for import into BattleScry. Any that are None emit empty.
    try:
        _hp = cmb.hp
        _mx = cmb.max_hp
        _acv = cmb.ac
        _hd = "1" if cmb.is_hidden else ""
        if _hp is not None or _mx is not None or _acv is not None or _hd:
            cs_parts.append(sn + ":" + (str(_hp) if _hp is not None else "") + ":" + (str(_mx) if _mx is not None else "") + ":" + (str(_acv) if _acv is not None else "") + ":" + _hd)
    except:
        pass
    if loc:
        tparts.append(sn + "|" + loc + "|" + sz_code.upper() + "|" + cl_code + "|" + ht_n + "|" + tk)
        # Build overlay entries: name~ovStr[@aim]
        for num, ov_str in ov_fields.items():
            aim_target = aim_fields.get(num, "")
            entry = sn + "~" + ov_str
            if aim_target:
                entry += "@" + aim_target.replace(" ", "%20")
            ovs.append(entry)
    else:
        # Unplaced - still capture overlays attached to them
        for num, ov_str in ov_fields.items():
            aim_target = aim_fields.get(num, "")
            entry = sn + "~" + ov_str
            if aim_target:
                entry += "@" + aim_target.replace(" ", "%20")
            ovs.append(entry)
        np_parts.append(sn)
    # Full notes for round-trip (preserves any field BS doesn't model)
    if note:
        clean = note.lstrip("# ").strip()
        fn_notes.append(sn + "~" + clean)
    # Init order capture
    try:
        if cmb.init is not None:
            ip_parts.append(sn + ":" + str(cmb.init))
    except:
        pass
    # Init group capture
    try:
        _grp = cmb.group
        if _grp:
            gname = str(_grp)
            if gname:
                gkey = gname.replace(" ", "%20")
                if gkey not in ig_parts:
                    ig_parts[gkey] = []
                ig_parts[gkey].append(sn)
    except:
        pass

# Saved tokens / maps / battles from uvars (preserved across round-trips).
# st= comes from mapTokens (shared with Croebh's !map -savetoken). tl= comes from bscry_tokenLabels (BS-only metadata, joined to mapTokens for the shortcode).
saved_tokens_str = ""
saved_maps_str = ""
map_thumbs_str = ""
saved_battles_str = ""
tl_string = ""
mt_parsed = {}
try:
    mt_raw = get_uvar("mapTokens") or "{}"
    mt_parsed = load_json(mt_raw)
    if not mt_parsed:
        mt_parsed = {}
except:
    mt_parsed = {}
# Format st= as name:code;name:code from mapTokens dict. Names with spaces become underscores per BS hash convention.
try:
    st_entries = []
    for k, v in mt_parsed.items():
        ks = str(k).strip().replace(" ", "%20")
        vs = str(v).strip()
        if ks and vs:
            st_entries.append(ks + ":" + vs)
    saved_tokens_str = ";".join(st_entries)
except:
    pass
try:
    mb_raw = get_uvar("mapBackgrounds") or "{}"
    mb_parsed = load_json(mb_raw)
    if not mb_parsed:
        mb_parsed = {}
    # sm= carries only the names. Full state stays in mapBackgrounds; load via `!bscry loadmap <name>`.
    # tm= carries thumb URLs (OTFBM URLs) keyed by name, for BS to preview saved maps before loading.
    # Format: name1|encoded_url1;;name2|encoded_url2. Thumbs are already percent-encoded by BS (via
    # encodeURIComponent) so URL chars don't break the URL hash. BS decodes on receive.
    sm_names = []
    tm_entries = []
    for k, v in mb_parsed.items():
        ks = str(k).strip().replace(" ", "%20")
        if ks:
            sm_names.append(ks)
            if v:
                _thumb = v.get("thumb", "") if v else ""
                if _thumb:
                    tm_entries.append(ks + "|" + str(_thumb))
    saved_maps_str = ";".join(sm_names)
    map_thumbs_str = ";;".join(tm_entries)
except:
    map_thumbs_str = ""
    pass
try:
    mbat_raw = get_uvar("mapBattles") or "{}"
    mbat_parsed = load_json(mbat_raw)
    if not mbat_parsed:
        mbat_parsed = {}
    # sb= carries only the names. Full state stays in mapBattles; load via `!bscry loadbattle <name>`.
    sb_names = []
    for k in mbat_parsed.keys():
        ks = str(k).strip().replace(" ", "%20")
        if ks:
            sb_names.append(ks)
    saved_battles_str = ";".join(sb_names)
except:
    pass
# Build tl= by joining bscry_tokenLabels (metadata) with mapTokens (for the shortcode that's already in st=).
# tl format: name|orig|text|size|color|bg|pos (7 fields; shortcode lives in st= for the same name).
try:
    tl_raw = get_uvar("bscry_tokenLabels") or "{}"
    tl_parsed = load_json(tl_raw)
    if not tl_parsed:
        tl_parsed = {}
    tl_entries = []
    for name, meta in tl_parsed.items():
        ns = str(name).strip().replace(" ", "%20")
        if not ns or not meta:
            continue
        text_field = str(meta.get("text", "")).replace(" ", "%20")
        tl_entries.append("|".join([
            ns,
            str(meta.get("orig", "")),
            text_field,
            str(meta.get("size", "M")),
            str(meta.get("color", "w")),
            str(meta.get("bg", "bk")),
            str(meta.get("pos", "bc")),
        ]))
    tl_string = ";".join(tl_entries)
except:
    tl_string = ""

parts = []
if gs:
    parts.append("g=" + gs)
if opts:
    parts.append("o=" + opts)
if bg:
    parts.append("bg=" + bg)
if vw:
    parts.append("vw=" + vw)
if tparts:
    parts.append("t=" + ";".join(tparts))
if ovs:
    parts.append("ov=" + ";".join(ovs))
if np_parts:
    parts.append("np=" + ";".join(np_parts))
if walls:
    parts.append("w=" + walls)
if fow:
    parts.append("fw=" + fow)
if objs:
    obs = objs.replace("/", ";").replace("; ", ";").replace(", ", ";")
    parts.append("ob=" + obs)
if fn_notes:
    parts.append("fn=" + ";;".join(fn_notes))
if saved_tokens_str:
    parts.append("st=" + saved_tokens_str)
if saved_maps_str:
    parts.append("sm=" + saved_maps_str)
if map_thumbs_str:
    parts.append("tm=" + map_thumbs_str)
if saved_battles_str:
    parts.append("sb=" + saved_battles_str)
if tl_string:
    parts.append("tl=" + tl_string)
if ig_parts:
    ig_str = ";".join([k + ":" + ",".join(v) for k, v in ig_parts.items()])
    parts.append("ig=" + ig_str)
if ip_parts:
    parts.append("ip=" + ";".join(ip_parts))
if cs_parts:
    parts.append("cs=" + ";".join(cs_parts))
data = "&".join(parts)
TOOL = "https://www.battlescry.com/"
encoded = data.replace("|", "%7C").replace(")", "%29").replace("(", "%28").replace("{", "%7B").replace("}", "%7D").replace(" ", "%20")
# Loadmap success marker - BS reads this to show a "loaded successfully" modal, then strips it
# from the URL bar via history.replaceState. Not stored in bscry_load uvar (so it doesn't persist).
url_hash = encoded
if is_loadmap and loadmap_status and loadmap_status.startswith("\u2705") and loadmap_name:
    _lm_safe = str(loadmap_name).replace(" ", "%20")
    url_hash = encoded + ("&" if encoded else "") + "_lm=" + _lm_safe
elif is_loadbattle and loadbattle_status and loadbattle_status.startswith("\u2705") and loadbattle_name:
    _lb_safe = str(loadbattle_name).replace(" ", "%20")
    url_hash = encoded + ("&" if encoded else "") + "_lb=" + _lb_safe
# Channel id, so BattleScry can tell two games open in the same browser apart. URL only, not BASE.
try:
    url_hash = url_hash + ("&" if url_hash else "") + "ch=" + str(ctx.channel.id)
except:
    pass
url = TOOL + "#" + url_hash

# Store new BASE for next round-trip (whatever state is current now). Without the _lm/_lb marker -
# that's transient UI signal, not state.
try:
    c.set_metadata(_base_key, encoded)
except:
    pass
set_uvar("bscry_load", encoded)

# ============================================================
# RETURN - apply embed or standard !bscry embed
# ============================================================
if is_apply:
    updated_str = ", ".join(apply_status_parts) if apply_status_parts else "No changes"
    n_conf = len(conflicts)
    edit_link = "[Click to keep editing in BattleScry →](" + url + ")"
    if secret:
        # Hide details - just counts. "map" is a bare label with no leading count, so it is
        # counted as one item rather than parsed as a number.
        total_items = 0
        for p in apply_status_parts:
            try:
                total_items += int(p.split(" ")[0])
            except:
                total_items += 1
        desc = "✅ BattleScry changes applied\nUpdated: " + str(total_items) + " item" + ("s" if total_items != 1 else "")
        if n_conf:
            desc += "\n⚠ " + str(n_conf) + " conflict" + ("s" if n_conf != 1 else "") + " (current map takes precedence)"
        desc += "\n\n" + edit_link
        embed_str = 'embed -title "🔮 BattleScry - Applied" -desc "' + desc + '" -color 0x22c55e -footer "Secret Mode - change details hidden"'
        # If new combatants were added, emit !i add commands first via multiline output.
        # They run before the embed shows, so the embed reflects the post-add state.
        if nc_followup_cmds:
            return "multiline\n" + "\n".join(nc_followup_cmds) + "\n!" + embed_str
        return embed_str
    else:
        desc = "✅ BattleScry changes applied\nUpdated: " + updated_str
        if n_conf:
            desc += "\n\n⚠ " + str(n_conf) + " conflict" + ("s" if n_conf != 1 else "") + " (current map takes precedence):"
            for cat, msg in conflicts[:8]:
                desc += "\n• " + msg
            if n_conf > 8:
                desc += "\n• ...and " + str(n_conf - 8) + " more"
        desc += "\n\n" + edit_link
        # OTFBM map image
        map_img = ""
        try:
            using(m='43a980ab-fcae-4baa-9d66-260b2b0d8672')
            m.load_data()
            map_img = m.get_link()
        except:
            map_img = ""
        # If BS sent free-floating overlay shortcodes, insert them as "*<shortcode>/" path
        # segments before the URL's query string. OTFBM renders these inline. They don't persist:
        # the next !map view regenerates the URL without them.
        if ff_str and map_img:
            ff_parts = []
            for _sc in ff_str.split(";"):
                _sc = _sc.strip()
                if _sc:
                    ff_parts.append("*" + _sc)
            if ff_parts:
                _ff_path = "/".join(ff_parts)
                if "?" in map_img:
                    _pre, _post = map_img.split("?", 1)
                    map_img = _pre.rstrip("/") + "/" + _ff_path + "/?" + _post
                else:
                    map_img = map_img.rstrip("/") + "/" + _ff_path
        cmd = 'embed -title "🔮 BattleScry - Applied" -desc "' + desc + '" -color 0x22c55e -footer "BattleScry v0.2.48"'
        if map_img:
            cmd += ' -image "' + map_img + '"'
        # If new combatants were added, emit !i add commands first via multiline output.
        # The commands run before the embed shows, so by the time the user sees the apply summary,
        # the new combatants are already in initiative. Duplicate-name protection is in the parser
        # so re-pasting the same apply twice is safe (subsequent runs skip already-added names).
        if nc_followup_cmds:
            return "multiline\n" + "\n".join(nc_followup_cmds) + "\n!" + cmd
        return cmd
else:
    # Standard !bscry embed (or loadmap result, which also uses this path with loadmap_status set)
    link = "# [Click to edit current map in BattleScry](" + url + ")"
    short = data if len(data) < 1000 else data[:997] + "..."
    map_link = ""
    try:
        using(m='43a980ab-fcae-4baa-9d66-260b2b0d8672')
        m.load_data()
        map_link = m.get_link()
    except:
        map_link = ""
    thumb = ' -thumb "' + map_link + '"' if map_link else ""
    if is_loadbattle:
        title = "🔮 BattleScry - Loaded Battle"
    elif is_loadmap:
        title = "🔮 BattleScry - Loaded Map"
    else:
        title = "🔮 BattleScry"
    desc_parts = [link]
    if bad_names:
        desc_parts.append("\u26a0 Not shown in BattleScry: " + ", ".join(bad_names) + ". Rename them without ; or | to place them on the map.")
    if loadmap_status:
        desc_parts.insert(0, loadmap_status)
    if loadbattle_status:
        desc_parts.insert(0, loadbattle_status)
    desc = "\n\n".join(desc_parts)
    if is_loadmap or is_loadbattle:
        out = 'embed -title "' + title + '" -desc "' + desc + '"' + thumb + ' -color 0x22c55e -footer "BattleScry v0.2.48"'
    else:
        out = 'embed -title "' + title + '" -desc "' + desc + '"' + thumb + ' -f "How to Use|#1: Click the link above to open the map in your browser (desktop or phone).\n#2: Move tokens, add overlays, edit the map.\n#3: Press Copy for Discord.\n#4: Paste it back here." -color 0xf59e0b -footer "BattleScry v0.2.48"'
    return out
</drac2>